      "correct": "4",
      "solution": "For find the opposite surface of 'K', we need to compare the common surface in the given dices,\n\nSo, From Dice 2 and Dice 3,\n\nWhen we move in clockwise direction starting from K we get;\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/b3b625dc46ccfeed1c91bd6a32f54cb05e296c923b5a841cad3731ff7fc23a20.png] \n\nIn dice 2, K is adjacent to N and M.\n\nIn dice 3, K is adjacent to L and P.\n\n→ K ⇔ K; M ⇔ L; N ⇔ P\n\nSo, the remaining 'O' will be the opposite face of 'K'.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"O\".",
