      "solution": "For find the opposite surface of 'Q', we need to compare the common surface in the given dices,\n\nSo, From Dice 2 and Dice 3,\n\nWhen we move in clockwise direction starting from P we get;\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/22cf6dba3cd649f2c87cfe9653488632b237062d2aec1c294ce5d949e865ceb8.png] \n\nIn dice 2 P is adjacent to S and U.\n\nIn dice 3, P is adjacent to R and T.\n\n→ P ⇔ P; U ⇔ R; S ⇔ T\n\nSo, the remaining 'P' will be the opposite face of 'Q'.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"P\".",
